614.docs:
# New (w/ Alternative Thousands Separator).

Nicely stringify a `u64` with a specific thousands separator (instead of the default comma).

## Examples

```
use dactyl::{NiceSeparator, NiceU64};

let num: u64 = 54321;

// Commas are used by default.
assert_eq!(
    NiceU64::from(num).as_str(),
    "54,321",
);

// Other contexts might prefer, say, underscores…
assert_eq!(
    NiceU64::with_separator(
        num,
        NiceSeparator::Underscore,
    ).as_str(),
    "54_321",
);
```

